From d99de711092384593dd9f3eb7d90a13d2a8ae01d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4pp4
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:47:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Network: use an own translation domain

The network panel has many messages from newer GNOME Settings and
NetworkManager that the Ubuntu language packs do not translate in
unity-control-center. Their translations in /usr/share/locale-langpack
take precedence over /usr/share/locale, so another package cannot add
the missing ones to the unity-control-center domain.

Translate the panel, the connection editor, the wireless security
widgets and the desktop file in the unity-control-center-network domain
instead.

Signed-off-by: c4pp4
